\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces McCrary density test of the incumbent vote margin. The vertical dashed line marks the 50\% electoral threshold. The distribution is smooth and continuous at the cutoff ($\hat  {\theta } = -0.0122$, $p = 0.884$), consistent with the absence of systematic vote-margin manipulation. The x-axis spans $-0.25$ to $0.5$ because no observations fall below $-0.25$.}}{6}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mccrary}{{9}{6}{McCrary density test of the incumbent vote margin. The vertical dashed line marks the 50\% electoral threshold. The distribution is smooth and continuous at the cutoff ($\hat {\theta } = -0.0122$, $p = 0.884$), consistent with the absence of systematic vote-margin manipulation. The x-axis spans $-0.25$ to $0.5$ because no observations fall below $-0.25$}{figure.caption.14}{}}
